body:
@kleonc 
The TileMap editor needs to assure valid outline output.

Ideally the entire option to create even-odd outlines with the TileMap cell editor should be removed in the first place. Those inner-outlines will always break when stack with other objects due to even-odd interpretation flips. They are a stability hazard and the reason why the more modern parts of the navigation system stopped supporting them entirely. Unfortunately the NavigationPolygon resource and some other places are still full of legacy comp crap that allows even-odd outlines which can't be fully removed. That is the entire reason why the traversable outlines part of the navmesh baking still uses them while the obstruction or obstacle parts don't.
